      "aliases": [
        "CVE-2026-97045"
      ],
      "summary": "Check all ancestor namespace transitions when rendering raw text in html in golang.org/x/net",
      "details": "In childTextNodesAreLiteral, walking up the tree previously stopped at the nearest foreign ancestor once an HTML integration point was found. However, that integration point may itself be a descendant of an element that was foster-parented into a foreign namespace (such as <mglyph> or <malignmark> fostered under <mtext>), causing a parser to resolve the subtree in a different foreign namespace upon re-parsing the rendered output.\n\nContinue walking the full ancestor chain and verify that every transition from a non-empty namespace occurs at an HTML integration point before emitting literal text.",
      "affected": [
        {
          "package": {
            "name": "golang.org/x/net",
            "ecosystem": "Go"
          },
          "ranges": [
